WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.165 --> 00:00:02.135
- You have to have your schedule so,

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.860
you really have to plan your day well.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.090
And I always like to make
some thing different.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:07.514
At least, different from myself.

00:00:07.514 --> 00:00:09.530
I always follow my heart with what I do.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:10.435
- [Audience Member] Do you have a routine,

00:00:10.435 --> 00:00:12.379
do you work out every day, what's the?

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:13.212
- What's the deal, what's the deal?

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:14.045
- Yeah.

00:00:14.045 --> 00:00:14.878
(laughs)

00:00:14.878 --> 00:00:15.738
- I'm actually a robot.

00:00:15.738 --> 00:00:17.051
Everybody needs to
develop their own thing.

00:00:17.051 --> 00:00:19.018
I don't really look at other people.

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:21.601
(trance music)

00:00:22.863 --> 00:00:24.441
- Hello Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:24.441 --> 00:00:26.978
My one word is believe
and I believe in people

00:00:26.978 --> 00:00:29.135
more than they believe in themselves.

00:00:29.135 --> 00:00:32.055
And my sincere hope is
that if you see in yourself

00:00:32.055 --> 00:00:35.356
what I see in you, you'll be
able to change the planet.

00:00:35.356 --> 00:00:36.844
So to help you on your journey today

00:00:36.844 --> 00:00:38.324
we're going to learn
from one of the greatest

00:00:38.324 --> 00:00:41.014
DJs of all time, Tiësto, and my take

00:00:41.014 --> 00:00:43.675
on his top ten rules for success.

00:00:43.675 --> 00:00:45.459
Rule number four is my personal favorite

00:00:45.459 --> 00:00:47.938
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:47.938 --> 00:00:49.648
Also as you're watching
if you hear something

00:00:49.648 --> 00:00:50.888
that really resonates with you

00:00:50.888 --> 00:00:52.509
please leave down the comments below

00:00:52.509 --> 00:00:53.875
and put quotes around it so other people

00:00:53.875 --> 00:00:55.693
can be inspired by it as well.

00:00:55.693 --> 00:00:56.849
And if you leave it within the first

00:00:56.849 --> 00:00:58.724
couple hours of this video going live,

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:02.807
you have a chance to win
one of two daily prizes.

00:01:04.859 --> 00:01:07.859
(inspiration music)

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.962
- I mean it depends,
if I have some time off

00:01:16.962 --> 00:01:18.765
I always take time for music so,

00:01:18.765 --> 00:01:22.610
for me it's different I think
but when I'm touring everyday,

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:23.701
I have actually more routine

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.250
than when I'm not touring everyday.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.584
So you have to have your schedule.

00:01:28.584 --> 00:01:30.558
You really have to plan your day well.

00:01:30.558 --> 00:01:32.644
But if I have six weeks off,

00:01:32.644 --> 00:01:34.644
I'm pretty much all over the place.

00:01:34.644 --> 00:01:37.176
Yeah, you don't really have a schedule

00:01:37.176 --> 00:01:38.872
so you just do whatever.

00:01:38.872 --> 00:01:40.222
- [Interviewer] Yeah, and you waste time.

00:01:40.222 --> 00:01:42.723
- Yeah, but if you have a
really military schedule

00:01:42.723 --> 00:01:44.756
then you have to really
plan everything well.

00:01:44.756 --> 00:01:47.076
So that works better for me, actually.

00:01:47.076 --> 00:01:49.806
I run 2007-2008 after I released my

00:01:49.806 --> 00:01:51.548
"Elements of Life" album and I felt like

00:01:51.548 --> 00:01:54.572
you know I've been
playing this kind of music

00:01:54.572 --> 00:01:57.381
and DJing this kind of
music for so many years.

00:01:57.381 --> 00:01:59.950
And I was just like, I want
to try something different

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:02.293
because I felt I had everything done

00:02:02.293 --> 00:02:05.483
that's possible in the trance
world, where I came from.

00:02:05.483 --> 00:02:07.062
So I could keep on going making trance

00:02:07.062 --> 00:02:08.520
but then they all start sound the same

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.148
as everything I've done before.

00:02:10.148 --> 00:02:12.315
And I always like to
make something different.

00:02:12.315 --> 00:02:13.906
At least different from myself.

00:02:13.906 --> 00:02:16.392
And to push myself, I always like to

00:02:16.392 --> 00:02:19.535
yeah look for the next thing.

00:02:19.535 --> 00:02:21.916
And I moved to L.A. for a couple months

00:02:21.916 --> 00:02:26.517
and I heard the American
DJs play there and in Vegas

00:02:26.517 --> 00:02:28.315
and they were mashing up all the stuff

00:02:28.315 --> 00:02:29.707
and everything was possible.

00:02:29.707 --> 00:02:32.444
You could play like a dance
track and a hip-hop track

00:02:32.444 --> 00:02:34.654
and everybody loved everything.

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:37.277
That inspired me to
become more open-minded,

00:02:37.277 --> 00:02:39.065
to really get more influence by

00:02:39.065 --> 00:02:41.439
different styles of dance music.

00:02:41.439 --> 00:02:43.310
And that's where I become more like

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:45.127
the "Kaleidoscope" album, more like

00:02:45.127 --> 00:02:48.912
loose rock indie artists,
singer/songwriters.

00:02:48.912 --> 00:02:51.020
And try to make different kind of songs.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:51.853
- [Interviewer] How has it been?

00:02:51.853 --> 00:02:53.750
How has the journey been for you?

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.313
- It's been a rollercoaster journey.

00:02:56.313 --> 00:03:00.609
And yeah, it seems like
it's never ending, you know?

00:03:00.609 --> 00:03:02.598
Every year I think maybe
now it's going less good,

00:03:02.598 --> 00:03:05.436
but still everything is going great.

00:03:05.436 --> 00:03:06.410
I always seem to make the right

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:09.789
decisions at the right
time so far, in my career.

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:12.442
I always follow my heart with what I do

00:03:12.442 --> 00:03:16.193
and with the music and so far so good.

00:03:16.193 --> 00:03:17.668
And I'm just happy with everything that's

00:03:17.668 --> 00:03:19.991
happened to me in the last ten years.

00:03:19.991 --> 00:03:21.190
- [Audience Member] How do you keep

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:22.023
your energy and your health,

00:03:22.023 --> 00:03:24.164
every time I've seen you all these years,

00:03:24.164 --> 00:03:25.964
you have such...

00:03:25.964 --> 00:03:27.257
energy.

00:03:27.257 --> 00:03:29.508
Life has ups and downs,
you have break ups,

00:03:29.508 --> 00:03:30.672
you have business problems.

00:03:30.672 --> 00:03:32.591
Every time I see step on to that stage,

00:03:32.591 --> 00:03:34.557
it's like do you have a routine,

00:03:34.557 --> 00:03:36.816
do you workout every day, what's the?

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:37.740
- What's the deal, what's the deal?

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.056
(laughs)

00:03:39.056 --> 00:03:40.815
I'm actually a robot.

00:03:40.815 --> 00:03:43.648
(audience laughs)

00:03:44.813 --> 00:03:45.980
Born in space.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.061
But I think it's very important

00:03:50.061 --> 00:03:52.345
to just have the passion for it.

00:03:52.345 --> 00:03:53.847
You know, and everybody can see that.

00:03:53.847 --> 00:03:56.999
I'm just a real person
and I love the music.

00:03:56.999 --> 00:04:00.541
I love to perform, I love to
DJ, I love to talk about it.

00:04:00.541 --> 00:04:02.645
I think that's, if you love what you do,

00:04:02.645 --> 00:04:05.178
you'll never really get tired.

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:06.856
I think that's the most important thing.

00:04:06.856 --> 00:04:10.508
I think the new generation
DJs is very clean,

00:04:10.508 --> 00:04:14.103
very focused on their work
and focused on their careers.

00:04:14.103 --> 00:04:17.807
And you can't afford to do drugs on stage.

00:04:17.807 --> 00:04:20.226
For me that's always
the exception, I guess.

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:23.422
The Amy Winehouse of
the DJs somewhere but,

00:04:23.422 --> 00:04:25.967
I think in general it just
doesn't work like that.

00:04:25.967 --> 00:04:28.974
People, DJs know they have one chance,

00:04:28.974 --> 00:04:30.909
and one chance only so they have to

00:04:30.909 --> 00:04:33.365
make the most out of it.

00:04:33.365 --> 00:04:36.532
Yeah, you can't let that go to pieces.

00:04:37.702 --> 00:04:39.739
So it's just about being a good DJ,

00:04:39.739 --> 00:04:41.989
it's about the right music.

00:04:43.468 --> 00:04:44.878
Fight for every chance you get.

00:04:44.878 --> 00:04:46.939
I made it to the top and nobody

00:04:46.939 --> 00:04:48.496
can ever take that away from me anymore.

00:04:48.496 --> 00:04:50.335
So I feel less pressure
and actually, I been

00:04:50.335 --> 00:04:52.835
number one two years in a row.

00:04:53.827 --> 00:04:55.907
So that's even more crazier, and I'm like

00:04:55.907 --> 00:04:57.882
well if I'm not number one next year

00:04:57.882 --> 00:05:00.741
I'm still going to be a good DJ.

00:05:00.741 --> 00:05:03.025
No matter what you have,
no matter who you are,

00:05:03.025 --> 00:05:04.013
always try to be yourself.

00:05:04.013 --> 00:05:04.846
(record scratch)

00:05:04.846 --> 00:05:05.726
I want to do something special,

00:05:05.726 --> 00:05:06.670
because everyone always says well,

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.663
the DJs are the new rock stars.

00:05:08.663 --> 00:05:11.726
But in general, they're
still just playing clubs,

00:05:11.726 --> 00:05:14.571
and do whatever they want
and not really put out,

00:05:14.571 --> 00:05:16.769
put in a good show, so we had some

00:05:16.769 --> 00:05:20.090
Brazilian drums, some Asian guitars

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.775
and for me that was the most

00:05:22.775 --> 00:05:25.512
incredible experience I ever had as a DJ.

00:05:25.512 --> 00:05:28.707
In general, I like to
work with people who can

00:05:28.707 --> 00:05:32.628
bring something creative
and emotional value

00:05:32.628 --> 00:05:34.550
to the song so it doesn't really matter

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:36.808
if she's or he's famous or not,

00:05:36.808 --> 00:05:40.975
it's more like what extra can
he or she bring to the song.

00:05:41.894 --> 00:05:43.793
That's, to me, the more important thing.

00:05:43.793 --> 00:05:46.147
No, not really pressure but you know,

00:05:46.147 --> 00:05:48.561
everybody needs to do their own thing.

00:05:48.561 --> 00:05:49.928
I don't really look at other people

00:05:49.928 --> 00:05:52.776
or what they do, I don't
compare myself to anybody.

00:05:52.776 --> 00:05:54.983
I just want to make myself
the best possible show

00:05:54.983 --> 00:05:58.196
that fits me and fits my crowd.

00:05:58.196 --> 00:06:02.432
Lately more and more
people struggle, I think

00:06:02.432 --> 00:06:06.147
in dance music because
they're not creative anymore.

00:06:06.147 --> 00:06:08.852
I think too many people
just think commercially,

00:06:08.852 --> 00:06:13.052
only about money and not
try to innovate the music

00:06:13.052 --> 00:06:16.743
like they used to do even
three or four years ago.

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:19.998
(crowd cheering)

00:06:19.998 --> 00:06:21.132
- I can't wait to get in.

00:06:21.132 --> 00:06:22.155
That's why I'm here this early,

00:06:22.155 --> 00:06:23.815
to get a great spot in there.

00:06:23.815 --> 00:06:24.859
- We're from Luton.

00:06:24.859 --> 00:06:25.750
- Luton.

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:26.583
- Everybody here's from Luton.

00:06:26.583 --> 00:06:28.958
- Okay so you only come
here to see Tiësto?

00:06:28.958 --> 00:06:29.791
- Yep.

00:06:29.791 --> 00:06:31.710
- We've been looking forward
to this for two months.

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:33.746
- [Crowd] Tiësto! Tiësto! Tiësto!

00:06:33.746 --> 00:06:35.885
- He has the greatest
club set in the world, so.

00:06:35.885 --> 00:06:36.718
- We love him.

00:06:36.718 --> 00:06:38.502
- We love his bravery.

00:06:38.502 --> 00:06:40.850
- I never expected this, so I think

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:43.425
it's going to be really
good vibes tonight.

00:06:43.425 --> 00:06:46.548
- [Crowd] Tiësto! Tiësto! Tiësto!

00:06:46.548 --> 00:06:49.186
(crowd cheering and screaming)

00:06:49.186 --> 00:06:51.281
- Hello and welcome to Copenhagen.

00:06:51.281 --> 00:06:53.030
We are now standing in front of Parken

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:56.947
and we are going in to
see a fantastic concert.

00:06:58.146 --> 00:07:01.479
- Bandspotter.com, I like it. It's good.

00:07:04.849 --> 00:07:07.432
(trance music)

00:07:11.513 --> 00:07:12.487
- How is it to stand like one man

00:07:12.487 --> 00:07:14.181
in the middle of the crowd,

00:07:14.181 --> 00:07:15.295
like it's really gone to the moon.

00:07:15.295 --> 00:07:16.624
- Yeah.

00:07:16.624 --> 00:07:19.002
- You came from nothing
and then you're just like

00:07:19.002 --> 00:07:20.633
standing with your hands in the air.

00:07:20.633 --> 00:07:22.113
- I'm the American dream.

00:07:22.113 --> 00:07:24.972
- (laughs) Yeah but how does it feel?

00:07:24.972 --> 00:07:26.421
I mean, I can't imagine.

00:07:26.421 --> 00:07:27.356
- How does it feel?

00:07:27.356 --> 00:07:29.712
- You don't get shy or
anything before you start?

00:07:29.712 --> 00:07:32.312
- No, you get used to it, I mean not

00:07:32.312 --> 00:07:35.907
in the way that it's not exciting anymore.

00:07:35.907 --> 00:07:38.444
If you play for thousand
people or five thousand

00:07:38.444 --> 00:07:40.234
or ten thousand, it
doesn't matter anymore.

00:07:40.234 --> 00:07:42.817
You know, it's a lot of people.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:48.071
So you get really excited,
I mean it's amazing.

00:07:48.071 --> 00:07:51.929
To be there by yourself
and you play your tracks.

00:07:51.929 --> 00:07:53.216
- Okay, I can imagine that.

00:07:53.216 --> 00:07:54.167
(Line laughs)

00:07:54.167 --> 00:07:57.371
It's the biggest rush on earth.

00:07:57.371 --> 00:07:59.954
(trance music)

00:08:30.256 --> 00:08:31.590
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:32.714
I made this video this video because

00:08:32.714 --> 00:08:34.806
Mark Syria asked me to.

00:08:34.806 --> 00:08:35.989
If there's someone
you'd like me to profile

00:08:35.989 --> 00:08:38.228
in a future Top Ten,
please check out the link

00:08:38.228 --> 00:08:39.558
down in the description below

00:08:39.558 --> 00:08:42.684
and you can cast your vote
on who we should do next.

00:08:42.684 --> 00:08:45.219
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Ranya Rahim.

00:08:45.219 --> 00:08:46.786
Ranya, thank you so much for picking up

00:08:46.786 --> 00:08:48.461
a copy of my book "Your One Word"

00:08:48.461 --> 00:08:50.041
and posting about it on Instagram.

00:08:50.041 --> 00:08:51.980
I really, really, really
appreciate the support

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:53.172
and I hope you enjoyed the read.

00:08:53.172 --> 00:08:54.494
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:08:54.494 --> 00:08:56.116
I believe in you, I hope you continue

00:08:56.116 --> 00:08:59.840
to believe in yourself and
whatever your one word is.

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:02.257
Much love. I'll see you soon.

00:09:08.013 --> 00:09:09.674
- You can't plan the future, you know?

00:09:09.674 --> 00:09:11.249
You never know what's going to happen

00:09:11.249 --> 00:09:13.495
but I just decided for myself,

00:09:13.495 --> 00:09:14.790
as long as I really enjoy it

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:17.161
and don't see it as work I will continue.

00:09:17.161 --> 00:09:19.964
And as soon as I feel
like now it's getting

00:09:19.964 --> 00:09:23.637
boring or annoying then I'm
definitely going to stop.

